.\" Manual page for mew (v2.0.0). Written in classic man(7) macros:
.\" no pandoc, no scdoc — hand-rolled, like everything else here.
.\" Render with: MANWIDTH=80 man -l docs/mew.1 | col -b
.TH MEW 1 "2026-08-21" "mew v2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mew \- a modern alternative to cat
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mew
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.RI [ FILE ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mew
concatenates files and prints them to standard output.
It aims to be a modern alternative to
.BR cat (1):
when standard output is not a terminal it behaves like a plain filter,
and on a terminal it can present line numbers and colored highlights.
It has zero dependencies beyond a C compiler and the C standard library.
With no
.I FILE
arguments, or when
.I FILE
is
.BR \- ,
standard input is read.
.SH OPTIONS
Grouped like
.B \-\-help :
first the cat-classic filters, then presentation,
then information.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-number\-nonblank
Number nonempty output lines; overrides
.BR \-n .
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-show\-all
Equivalent to
.BR \-vET .
.TP
.BR \-e
Equivalent to
.BR \-vE .
.TP
.BR \-E ", " \-\-show\-ends
Display $ at end of each line.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-number
Number all output lines.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-squeeze\-blank
Suppress repeated empty output lines.
.TP
.BR \-t
Equivalent to
.BR \-vT .
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-show\-tabs
Display TAB characters as ^I.
.TP
.BR \-u
Ignored; accepted for POSIX compatibility.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-show\-nonprinting
Use ^ and M\- notation, except for LFD and TAB.
.TP
.BR "\-\-color[=\fIWHEN\fP]"
Colorize
.BR mew 's
own decorations.
.I WHEN
may be
.BR always ,
.BR auto ,
or
.BR never ;
the default is
.BR auto ,
which colors only when standard output is a terminal.
Note that
.B NO_COLOR
(see
.B ENVIRONMENT
below) also suppresses color.
.TP
.BR \-\-show\-range
Declared in this release but not implemented:
any invocation aborts with a usage error.
It is listed here so the option inventory stays complete;
see the project issue tracker for its planned
.IR RANGE \ ( START : END )
semantics.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of options and exit successfully.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit successfully.
.PP
Exit status and option behavior follow the conventions described below;
any option received but not listed here is rejected with a usage message.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error (unknown or invalid option) or I/O error
(missing or unreadable input file).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to any nonempty value, disables colored output
even when
.B \-\-color=always
would otherwise apply on a terminal.
.SH EXAMPLES
Number every line of a file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
mew \-n src/parser.c
.RE
.fi
.PP
Number only nonempty lines, squeeze runs of blanks:
.PP
.nf
.RS
mew \-bs notes.txt
.RE
.fi
.PP
Show tabs and ends explicitly while debugging whitespace:
.PP
.nf
.RS
mew \-ET Makefile
.RE
.fi
.PP
Reveal nonprinting characters in a suspicious file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
mew \-v dump.bin
.RE
.fi
.PP
Force color even through a pipe (e.g. for a pager that understands it):
.PP
.nf
.RS
mew \-\-color=always build.log | less \-R
.RE
.fi
.PP
Guarantee plain output for scripting, whatever the terminal:
.PP
.nf
.RS
mew \-\-color=never config.yml
.RE
.fi
.PP
Read from standard input, numbered:
.PP
.nf
.RS
curl \-s https://example.com | mew \-n
.RE
.fi
.PP
Concatenate several inputs into one stream:
.PP
.nf
.RS
mew header.txt body.txt footer.txt > out.txt
.RE
.fi
.SH INSTALLATION
The page you are reading ships with the source tree.
Build and install with:
.PP
.nf
.RS
make
make install          # PREFIX=/usr/local by default
.RE
.fi
.PP
Both
.B PREFIX
and
.B DESTDIR
are honored; the manual page lands in
.IR $PREFIX/share/man/man1/mew.1 .
Preview this page without installing:
.PP
.nf
.RS
make man
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cat (1),
.BR less (1)
